cff-version: 1.2.0
message: 'If you use ReuseProof CA, please cite it as below.'
title: 'ReuseProof CA Core — deterministic evidence-domain foundation for California OTNWS programs'
abstract: >-
  An initially read-only, hardware-neutral regulatory evidence and
  program-operations control plane for California local jurisdictions that
  elect to operate onsite treated nonpotable water system (OTNWS) programs.
  The current shipped slice is a headless TypeScript domain foundation:
  deterministic required-series coverage evaluation, readiness preflight and
  frozen report artifacts with hash-derived receipts.
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Chelsea
    family-names: Kelly-Reif
license: Apache-2.0
repository-code: 'https://github.com/ChelseaKR/reuseproof-ca-core'
url: 'https://github.com/ChelseaKR/reuseproof-ca-core'
keywords:
  - california
  - water-reuse
  - otnws
  - regulatory-evidence
  - civic-tech
  - typescript
# `version` mirrors the in-development version in package.json, which is the single source
# of truth; tests/release-claims.test.ts asserts the two agree. It was missing entirely,
# so this file gave a release date with nothing to attach it to.
#
# `date-released` is deliberately absent. It carried 2026-07-19 while `git tag --list` was
# empty here and on origin, no GitHub Release existed, and CHANGELOG.md said in terms that
# no version had been tagged. Citation tooling prints this field as the date the software
# was released, so anyone citing this project was handed a release date for a release that
# never happened; the date was real, it was just the date of something else.
# tests/release-claims.test.ts ties its presence to a tag naming the declared version, in
# both directions, so it returns the moment a release is cut and cannot be left out of one.
version: '0.1.0'
